WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.459
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Independence Spark.

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:20.919
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:24.794
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:28.670
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:37.713
There is a particular feeling that comes when you do a hard thing yourself. Not the whole thing. Your piece of it. It feels like a small light switching on.

00:00:37.713 --> 00:00:48.048
That feeling has a name in this room. We call it the spark. The spark is not about being the best. It is about the try being yours.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:59.675
A zipper that finally catches. A puzzle piece that turns the right way. The first step of a hard job, done by your own hands.

00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:04.842
The spark has a simple order. Try first. Then help is right there. Let me show you.

00:01:04.842 --> 00:01:16.469
Trying first does not mean the whole job. It means one step. The first step. Your step.

00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:28.096
Look at the step before you touch it. Turn it over in your mind. Where does it start? What does your hand do first?

00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:39.723
Then try — slowly. A slow try teaches your hands more than a fast grab. If the step does not work, you have learned something real about the step.

00:01:39.723 --> 00:01:50.058
A try that doesn't work is information. It is not a verdict about you. Every person who can do this thing once stood exactly where you are standing.

00:01:50.058 --> 00:01:51.350
And when a piece of it works — feel that. That steady, proud warmth is the spark. You made it. Nobody can hand you that feeling. It only comes from the try.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:02:02.977
Now hear the other half, because it matters just as much. Asking for help is never a failure. Not before the try, not after it, not ever.

00:02:02.977 --> 00:02:14.604
Help is a tool, like a step stool. Sometimes the wise move is the try. Sometimes the wise move is help first. Knowing which one — that is part of growing, too.

00:02:14.604 --> 00:02:23.647
And the spark is never a race. You are not measuring yourself against anyone else's hands. The only fair comparison is your own yesterday.

00:02:23.647 --> 00:02:24.939
Yesterday you could not. Today you tried. That distance — yours alone — is the whole size of the spark.

00:02:24.939 --> 00:02:33.982
One step. Your try. Help when you need it.

00:02:33.982 --> 00:02:40.441
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:40.441 --> 00:02:45.609
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:52.068
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:52.068 --> 00:02:58.527
You're ready for what's next.
